Description: the default of the config option telemetry "disabled", not "enabled":
 the patch of Fedora (extra-patch-telemetry-opt-in) takes "enabled" for an opt-in, and
 with no telemetry in the config file gh takes the default of the option, so without
 this one gh would still send telemetry where the user never chose it. Opting in:
 gh config set telemetry enabled, or GH_TELEMETRY=1 (or true, yes, on); log: print
 the payload instead of sending it.
Origin: azsupport/ports

--- a/internal/config/config.go
+++ b/internal/config/config.go
@@ -949,7 +949,7 @@
 	{
 		Key:           telemetryKey,
 		Description:   "whether telemetry is enabled, disabled, or logging",
-		DefaultValue:  "enabled",
+		DefaultValue:  "disabled",
 		AllowedValues: []string{"enabled", "disabled", "log"},
 		CurrentValue: func(c gh.Config, hostname string) string {
 			return c.Telemetry().Value
